  "id": "market-briefs-export-license",
  "title": "Export-License Review",
  "turns": [
    {
      "jobId": "6b752d58-6ff7-43f1-aef7-38cb5dcca09e",
      "question": "What did Galena Semiconductor say about export-license exposure, and which mitigations did it mention?",
      "submittedAt": "2026-09-29T20:32:05.678820Z",
      "completedAt": "2026-09-29T20:33:44.014466Z",
      "status": "success",
      "report": {
        "markdown": "Galena Semiconductor disclosed that it is **reviewing fictional export‑license requirements for a subset of its accelerators**. Management stressed that the review is still incomplete, but it identified two possible mitigations:\n\n* **Product reconfiguration** – adjusting the design or specifications of the affected accelerators.\n* **Regional mix changes** – shifting the geographic distribution of sales or production to reduce exposure.\n\nThese points come from the “Galena Reviews Export‑License Exposure” brief published on 2026‑08‑27 [1].\n\n## Sources\n\n- [1] Unstructured Retrieval evidence — 8 documents — evidence `hermes-receipt:d180753fb63ac49cfbe516eefc7254682d25dac0a7ea3fe7978c7747fa7b031c`",
        "citations": [
          {
